then use the conditional flow-matching interpolation of @lipman2023flowmatchinggenerativemodeling,

$ theta_t = (1-t) theta_0 + t theta_1. $

The network regresses the constant path velocity,

$ cal(L) = EE norm(v_psi(t,theta_t,Y) - (theta_1-theta_0))^2. $

This convention is used throughout: *$t=0$ is noise and $t=1$ is the target*.
At inference, the ODE $dif theta / dif t = v_psi(t,theta,Y)$ is integrated
from 0 to 1 with 96 Euler steps. Each independent initial noise produces one
posterior draw; all reported decoders use $S=100$ draws.

The condition encoder mean-pools time by a factor of 12, applies three
one-dimensional convolutional blocks, and maps the sensor sequence to a
192-dimensional vector. The vector field is a three-layer width-512 MLP over
